OL,3,AFight over fossil fuels leaves COP31
OL,4,Aclimate talks in deadlock
OL,5,
OL,6,FNegotiations at the COP31 UN climate
OL,7,Fsummit in Turkey are in deadlock,
OL,8,Fhaving run through the night, as
OL,9,Fcountries remain unable to agree on a
OL,10,Fnew global climate deal.
OL,12,FIn a late intervention on Friday, a
OL,13,Fgroup of countries led by France and
OL,14,FPanama pushed back against the draft
OL,15,Fagreement which included no reference
OL,16,Fto reducing the world's demand for
OL,17,Ffossil fuels.
OL,19,FSeparately, the Africa Group are
OL,20,Ffighting to get commitments on more
OL,21,Fmoney for adaptation, saying they did
OL,22,Fnot come to the COP "to beg".
OL,23,APub: 21-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
